        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "WdppP",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1500,
          "name": "notes",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1260,
          "content": "DEFERRED, NOT DISCARDED — the rows above describe the multi-tab design: a node holding several tabs, the tab bar replacing the chat header, and group actions moving onto the tabs. It is postponed, not dropped; the full design is kept in “Spec — Node → Tab → View · DEFERRED” and in the two backup chat frames.\n\nWHAT V1 DOES INSTEAD — nothing changes above the split. The chat header stays exactly as it renders today (WorkspaceHeader, surfaces/panes.rs:257): split glyph, auto-composed title, the group kebab, and the layout picker plus side-panel toggle on the right. The layout picker keeps its current scope — it splits the node, because a node is still one arrangement.\n\nTHE ONE CHANGE V1 MAKES — a pane can now hold a terminal instead of a chat, and each pane in a split carries the slimmed identity line below. That is the whole feature. Tabs become a clean additive step later precisely because nothing here has to be undone to get them.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BDjZ4",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1750,
          "name": "cap",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "VIEW ⋯ MENU — ALWAYS VISIBLE ON THE IDENTITY LINE",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "yPDMm",
          "x": 300,
          "y": 1750,
          "name": "cap",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "…AND THE VIEW GOES EMPTY — THAT IS WHERE A NEW ONE STARTS",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
