        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "yHFYd",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 540,
          "name": "cap_decisions",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "DECISIONS",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PMzuh",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 562,
          "name": "decisions",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "HEADER CLUSTERS — the left cluster is the session: icon · title · ⋯ · Stop · ⑂ Fork. The right cluster is the surface: split · drawer · side panel. Fork leaves the trailing group #60 gave it and sits beside Stop, so every right-hand glyph toggles a surface and every left-hand glyph acts on the session.\n\nONE DRAWER PER TAB — docked under the pane split, full width, never a cell of the split. #356 chose \"a terminal is a pane\" as the smallest shape; this supersedes that for in-tab terminals only. The chats keep the whole split, the shell appears beneath them and goes away without re-flowing anything.\n\nTOGGLE — ⌥F12 and the header icon. lucide panel-bottom, hollow at rest, raised pill while open (the layout picker's open treatment). It sits between the split glyph and the side-panel glyph, the order Codex uses. When the side panel is open its own collapse button still lives in the panel; the drawer's hide control lives in the strip, so the header never shows two active pills for one surface.\n\nENTRY POINTS RE-POINTED — the empty-pane placeholder's New terminal, the palette's New terminal, and ⌥F12 all open the drawer. A drawer with no shell spawns one at the focused pane's cwd by the #356 rule: focused sibling → project directory → default working dir → $HOME.\n\nHIDE IS NOT CLOSE — chevron / ⌥F12 hide the drawer and every shell keeps running; the chip's × kills that shell with the same foreground-process confirmation a pane terminal gets today; closing or archiving the tab closes all of its drawer shells. Archive all on a tab with drawer shells confirms, as it does for pane terminals.\n\nSEVERAL SHELLS, ONE VISIBLE — + adds a chip at the same cwd; chips switch the visible terminal; the active chip is raised. No split inside the drawer, no drag-reorder of chips in v1.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jVgu1",
          "x": 760,
          "y": 562,
          "name": "decisions_2",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 640,
          "content": "HEIGHT — drag the handle; clamp 120–600 px; default 280. Open/closed and height ride with the tab in the window-layout checkpoint, so a relaunch restores a tab the way it was left; drawer shells respawn like pane shells (fresh shell at the cwd, no replay, no scrollback).\n\nSESSION MODEL UNCHANGED — drawer shells are the same \"shell\" direct sessions #356 introduced: same spawn path, excluded from attention (never working / unread / needs-you), Shell exited card with Restart. They are parented to the tab, not placed in a pane, so the node reconciler never wraps them in a tab of their own and the sidebar never lists them.\n\nSIDEBAR UNCHANGED — New terminal from the Recent / project + menus still creates a terminal-only tab with the terminal in its pane; that tab offers no drawer (a standalone terminal has nothing to sit beneath).\n\nMIGRATION — a split that already holds a shell pane keeps working until that pane is closed; nothing is moved automatically and there is no Move to drawer action in v1.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE — a drawer in the mission workspace; changing ⌘D / ⇧⌘D (they keep growing the chat split); a terminal picker; per-chip rename.\n\nEMPTY PANE — New terminal leaves the placeholder; the drawer is the tab's terminal now, so an empty pane only ever asks for a chat. New chat is one accent button that carries its shortcut inline — \"⌘N  New chat\", reading the effective binding; ⌘N fills a focused empty pane before it falls back to opening a new tab (today it always opens a tab).",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "TQUPp",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 190,
          "name": "cap_header",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "HEADER — TWO CLUSTERS: THE LEFT ACTS ON THE SESSION, THE RIGHT TOGGLES A SURFACE. FORK MOVES LEFT, BESIDE STOP (WAS TRAILING, #60)",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
